#lang r7rs
;; r7rs-gc threads, stage A (docs/archive/r7rs-gc-threads-plan.md): the
;; emitted runtime's per-thread state is thread-local under the collector
;; (each thread registers its instances as roots), so two threads started
;; the way stdlib/thread starts them each see their own cancellation flag:
;; 10 means only the cancelled one saw it.  With that state shared, as it
;; was while the collector refused threads, both read the last thread's.
(import (scheme base) (scheme write) (turmeric tlsmod))
(display (tls-run)) (newline)
